fix:
Pre-allocate a single mutable builder (like `String::with_capacity`) and use a collecting parameter pattern (or `write!` macro) to accumulate data without reallocation.
```rust
pub fn build_csv(rows: &[Vec<String>]) -> String {
    let mut csv = String::with_capacity(rows.len() * 128); // Pre-allocated
    for row in rows {
        csv.push_str(&row.join(","));
        csv.push_str("\n");
    }
    csv
}
```
